A||||10||mrfiero||Borla exhaust is installed!||||10||
Z||000000||mrfiero||10-02-2000||07:15 PM||||I just got done installing a Borla system on my '88 GT and man what a difference!  While I was in there I removed the manifolds and ported out the restrictions.  I also replaced a severely cracked y-pipe (maybe that's where the code 32 was coming from?).<P>I would have finished up yesterday, but nobody stocks the exhaust manifold gaskets.  I even called up NAPA's Denver warehouse.....nothing.  Then I had an idea.....why not try using the gaskets from a Camaro 3.4?  I went to Auto Zone (a block from my house) and bought a set of 3.4 gaskets.  While they do look different, they worked and I'm happy.  The kicker was the price.....a set of Fel-Pro gaskets for a 2.8 Fiero was $22, this set of Fel-Pro 3.4 gaskets was $6!! <P>At any rate, the install went fairly smoothly and the result is phenomenal.....my GT now growls when I rev her up and the code 32 seems to have vanished. ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-03-2000||07:53 AM||||Did you repai the front fender, or is the Borla car different from the one you drove to Rutland?||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||10-03-2000||11:46 AM||||It's the same car I drove to the east coast (I only have 2 Fieros I drive...this one and my 16K mile "baby").  I have the parts to fix the fender/hood and will do that later this week.  I wanted to get the exhaust tightened up first.....the performance was pretty weak, but now it actually accelerates and sounds better.  <P>After I finish the body work I plan on starting a 3.4 build up.  I should have that ready to go and installed by next summer....just in time for the show!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>BTW Larry.....I saw your GT at Bob's place and decided to reacquire my steering wheel.  I hope you don't mind.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroparts.com||10-03-2000||11:49 AM||||MR FIERO<P>Glad to see you like your Borla system, well <BR>worth it ah?  ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-03-2000||04:24 PM||||Bob said you were eyeing my 88. The last time I saw it there was no engine in it and it was rather dusty.  The insides were sort of all over the place.  I'm anticipating the Nolan Concepts powder coated plenum and valve covers were there as well as the chromed throttle body.  Bob told me he was waiting for some special clamps.  It should be a nice car once its done.  I'm almost ready to take a ride out there just to see it.  The 87 is going into storage soon,  winter is arriving this week.<P>I still have the ugly one I took out of the 88.  Who does leather wheel reupolstry besides the Fiero Store? I saw nothing on Mr. Mikes web site.||||reg||1
